    "focal_turn_index": 7,
    "prior_context": {
      "alternative_citation_allowed": false,
      "annotated_sentence_text": "[Turn 6 USER]\ne126\tThat's really hard to hear.\ne127\tI've been telling myself for six months that it was necessary because of the sleepover lie.\ne128\tAnd yes, now it's been \"justified\" by what I found.\ne129\tBut I hear what you're saying.\ne130\tCan we go back to her?\ne131\tIt's day four.\ne132\tShe came down for dinner tonight, first time.\ne133\tDidn't look at me but ate at the table.\ne134\tSaid \"can I go now\" after ten minutes.\ne135\tI said \"yes, I love you\" and she nodded and left.\ne136\tThat's progress, right?\n[Turn 6 ASSISTANT]\ne137\tThat's progress.\ne138\tDon't overinterpret it but don't underestimate it either.\ne139\tShe came down, she ate, she nodded when you said you loved her.\ne140\tShe is signaling that the thaw is starting.\ne141\tWhat I would NOT do tonight: say anything else to her.\ne142\tDon't try to follow up.\ne143\tDon't ask her to talk.\ne144\tDon't leave her another note.\ne145\tThe risk right now is pushing too hard too early and getting her to retreat.\ne146\tLet her lead the next step.\ne147\tWhat I would do: tomorrow, text her something very low-stakes and unrelated.\ne148\tNot about the guy, not about rules, not about how you're feeling.\ne149\tSomething like \"your sweatshirt is in the dryer\" or \"I'm going to the grocery, want anything.\"\ne150\tTreat normal as the goal.\ne151\tShe needs to see that the relationship can go back to functioning without the thing being solved yet.\ne152\tThe thing being solved (the guy, the phone, the conversation about trust) will come later.\ne153\tRight now the job is making her feel that home is safe and predictable while she's in shame.\ne154\tKids in shame need routine more than processing.",
